{"id": "EUVD-2026-48796", "enisaUuid": "76d6a5e4-64cc-3487-ab18-5580d72a77a8", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\n6lowpan: fix NHC entry use-after-free on error path\n\nlowpan_nhc_do_uncompression() looks up an NHC descriptor while holding\nlowpan_nhc_lock.  If the descriptor has no uncompress callback, the error\npath drops the lock before printing nhc->name.\n\nlowpan_nhc_del() removes descriptors under the same lock and then relies\non synchronize_net() before the owning module can be unloaded.  That only\nwaits for net RX RCU readers.  lowpan_header_decompress() is also exported\nand can be reached from callers that are not necessarily covered by the net\ncore RX critical section, for example the Bluetooth 6LoWPAN L2CAP receive\npath.\n\nThis leaves a race where one task drops lowpan_nhc_lock in the error path,\nanother task unregisters and frees the matching descriptor after\nsynchronize_net() returns, and the first task then dereferences nhc->name\nfor the warning.\n\nWith the post-unlock window widened, KASAN reports:\n\n  BUG: KASAN: slab-use-after-free in lowpan_nhc_do_uncompression+0x1f4/0x220\n  Read of size 8\n  lowpan_nhc_do_uncompression\n  lowpan_header_decompress\n\nFix this by printing the warning before dropping lowpan_nhc_lock, so the\ndescriptor name is read while unregister is still excluded.  The malformed\npacket is still rejected with -ENOTSUPP.", "datePublished": "2026-07-25T08:51:21", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T20:38:30", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9c2f5c0829a8c8b904dae36be6d8056b719ac605", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/80b5c8779acee0550845394fb3e5176a398aa24c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cc27aea4d454abfb385ee2c9499c78b96db9b728", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a8e3a94711134e898c6021a6b77374efa91b3639", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/593b78bb3c7ef0c6e9ae6fdf5afa80a5f7573168", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0beccbcf50de125be5520d0ffc59af4bb8655482", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b713aa0cc344f10f7a9928a230b5f5e780d04078", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1720db928e5a58ca7d75ac1d514c3b73fd7061a7"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-64452", "GHSA-c2hf-fh99-25vq"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02658ad9-fa98-3db9-a75c-f4ff9f6d8f15", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "92aa7c65d295f3cbb96904afe335f683e55584b8 <9c2f5c0829a8c8b904dae36be6d8056b719ac605"}, {"id": "146156ab-8763-36db-b30f-00ac9660a8a1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.1"}, {"id": "3ca3f292-fb58-3647-b59c-bbdc28658bc6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "5f4923f6-c491-378a-9a4c-327a70931dfe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.4"}, {"id": "617d9b39-e2a6-3e8c-8e14-ecb93c4f018e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "92aa7c65d295f3cbb96904afe335f683e55584b8 <1720db928e5a58ca7d75ac1d514c3b73fd7061a7"}, {"id": "619d1a92-4090-3117-84e6-6dd8c9ba2ccf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "92aa7c65d295f3cbb96904afe335f683e55584b8 <80b5c8779acee0550845394fb3e5176a398aa24c"}, {"id": "79e06159-dd4a-3ba6-b674-667163396912", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "92aa7c65d295f3cbb96904afe335f683e55584b8 <a8e3a94711134e898c6021a6b77374efa91b3639"}, {"id": "81ea3159-1031-329b-a10c-249601548ed6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "92aa7c65d295f3cbb96904afe335f683e55584b8 <593b78bb3c7ef0c6e9ae6fdf5afa80a5f7573168"}, {"id": "91889130-67ec-36ac-b88c-eab2aede70fc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "92aa7c65d295f3cbb96904afe335f683e